config AMLOGIC_C5_NATIVE_DISPLAY
	bool "C5 native VPU/HDMI integration (experimental)"
	depends on AMLOGIC_C5_DISPLAY_RESOURCES
	depends on DRM = y && I2C = y && AMLOGIC_CPU_INFO = y
	depends on DMA_CMA && REGMAP_MMIO
	depends on !AMLOGIC_MEDIA_ENABLE
	select PHY_MESON_S7D_HDMI
	select RESET_S7D_VPU
	select DRM_KMS_HELPER
	select DRM_GEM_DMA_HELPER
	select DRM_DISPLAY_HELPER
	select DRM_DISPLAY_HDMI_HELPER
	select DRM_BRIDGE_CONNECTOR
	select SND_SOC_HDMI_CODEC if SND_SOC
	help
	  Build the S7D VPU execution path and native RGB8 TMDS bridge, with
	  DRM EDID/SCDC helpers, CCF consumers and generic PHY ownership.
	  Static device trees and built-in drivers only; unbind is suppressed.
	  Register one CRTC, linear RGB primary, linear NV12/NV21 VD1/VD2 video and
	  shared OSD2 cursor/overlay planes, and an HDMI connector.
	  Cursor and RGB overlay cannot be visible together. Video is progressive
	  8-bit SDR with BT.601/709 limited/full-range conversion.
	  Each local OSD scaler supports up to 4x enlargement and 2:1 reduction,
	  including simultaneous primary and RGB overlay scaling. Linear RGB
	  scaling requires opaque pixels and input width up to 1920.
	  VD1 supports up to 4x enlargement and 8x downscaling
	  in 1080p output modes. Linear video and OSD scaling may run together
	  within a checked combined clock budget. VD2 is unscaled up to 2048x1080;
	  VD1 and VD2 together exclude OSD2. VD2 does not combine with AFBC.
	  AFBC ABGR8888 supports a primary or OSD2 overlay up to 4096x2160,
	  with opaque global alpha and optional premultiplied pixel alpha.
	  AFBC scaling uses the same local OSD limits and uncropped source.
	  An AFBC primary can use a linear OSD2 cursor or
	  overlay. Only one AFBC surface is active. An opaque unscaled AFBC
	  primary can combine with unscaled video up to 1080p at 148.5 MHz;
	  joint primary/video changes require a stopped modeset.
	  Requires retained firmware output on S7D revision B, with SDR RGB8 TMDS up to 594 MHz.
	  Do not enable with legacy media/display writers. System sleep supports
	  s2idle after native takeover, retaining the shared display domain.
	  HDMI PCM uses SND_SOC_HDMI_CODEC with SND_SOC_MESON_S7D_HDMI_AUDIO
	  and SND_SOC_ODROIDC5. Deep sleep, hibernation and cold HDMI SRAM
	  initialization are not supported.
